<section class="marketing-section">
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Staff rehearse realistic guest interactions on their own time, instead
    of learning live in front of a paying table. Every rep gets immediate
    feedback — not a script to memorize, but real practice at handling
    whatever a guest actually says.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="marketing-section">
  <h2>What staff train on</h2>
  <ul class="marketing-feature-list">
    <li><strong>Menu</strong> — know the food and drink list cold, not just skim it once.</li>
    <li><strong>Off-Menu knowledge</strong> — answer the questions that aren't printed anywhere.</li>
    <li><strong>Recommendations &amp; Pairings</strong> — guide a table with confidence, not guesswork.</li>
    <li><strong>Handling Complaints</strong> — stay composed and on-brand when a table pushes back.</li>
    <li><strong>Upselling</strong> — offer more without it feeling like a pitch.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="marketing-section">
  <h2>Why it matters for your restaurant</h2>
  <p>
    Consistent training means consistent service, shift after shift, no
    matter who's on the floor. Staff walk into a shift already prepared —
    without pulling anyone off the floor to learn — and that readiness
    shows up directly in the guest experience and in who comes back.
  </p>
</section>

